$ w --why tungsten

  ◆ tungsten · W · 74
  │ atomic mass    183.84 u
  │ density        19.3 g/cm³
  │ melting point  3421.85 °C
  │ boiling point  5554.85 °C
  │ state          solid
  │ category       transition metal
  │ discovered     1783
  │ named          From Swedish tung
  │   sten, 'heavy stone'. Its symbol W
  │   is from wolfram, after the ore
  │   wolframite: German wolf rahm,
  │   'wolf's cream', from Agricola's
  │   Latin lupi spuma, 'wolf's froth',
  │   because the ore devoured tin
  │   during smelting as a wolf devours
  │   sheep.

